        "text": {
            "description_html": "<b>Omnia 71000ACA, Solid Brass Patio Door Trim Set</b>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nThe classic styling of Omnia's 71000 series multipoint trim grants it an elegance that is only enhanced through the addition of one of the beautiful lever design options--all of which are just as sophisticated as the patio trim itself. These solid brass leversets are for use with American Cylinder Above Lever (american profile lock cylinder above the door lever) type multipoint mortise locksets commonly found on swinging patio doors. Available in 4 finishes.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nThe <b>Thru-Bolts</b> are fixed at 8-1/2\" center to center and can not be modified. In some cases new thru-bolting holes must be drilled in your door. \r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nThis set does not come packaged with the multipoint lock mechanism (the vertical rods found in multipoint patio doors that secure the door to the frame) as those are typically preinstalled in multipoint doors and cannot be replaced. The multipoint trim set is intended to replace the original trim from G-U, Eagle, BiltBest, Hurd and others. The <b>Lock to Lever</b> distance is 3-5/8\" (92 mm).\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Also Available: Arched Patio Door Trim <a href=\"/products/arched-american-cylinder-patio-door-trim-set-omnia-71000acb\">with <b>American Cylinder Below</b> the lever</a> and <a href=\"/products/arched-european-cylinder-patio-door-trim-set-omnia-71000ecb\">with <b>European Cylinder</b></a></p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0766/1489/3857/files/LAU-74466-SM.jpg?v=1704354551\" width=\"500\" height=\"250\" border=\"0\" alt=\"71000ACA Multipoint Trim Sets dimensions\">\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>Specifications:</b> for Omnia 71000ACA Multipoint Trim Sets\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Material: Solid Brass Trim</li>\r\n<li>Lock to Lever Spacing: 3-5/8\" (92 mm) Center to Center</li>\r\n<li>Thru-Bolt Hole Spacing: 8-1/2\"  (216 mm) Center to Center</li>\r\n<li>Plate Height: 9-5/8\" (244 mm)</li>\r\n<li>Plate Width: 1-3/4\" (44 mm)</li>\r\n<li>Plate Projection: 1/2\" (12.5 mm)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>",
